a(1,'M1',11,48,'stat','Which equation is the most appropriate linear model for the data shown in the scatterplot?',['y = 0.2 + 2.25x','y = 0.2 − 2.25x','y = 2.25 + 0.2x','y = 2.25 − 0.2x'],'A','The data increase by about 2.25 units of y per unit x and extrapolate near y=0. The other choices have a negative or much smaller slope.',[90,150,550,555])
a(1,'M1',12,48,'rat',r'What is the x-intercept of \(y=\frac{21-x}{ax+b}\), where a and b are positive constants?',['(21, 0)','(0, −21)',r'\((0,\frac{21}{b})\)',r'\((-\frac{b}{a},0)\)'],'A','Set the numerator equal to zero: x=21. The denominator 21a+b is positive, so (21,0) is valid.')
a(1,'M1',13,49,'eq','A model estimates that a glacier moves between 17 and 24 centimeters per day. Which inequality gives possible values of x, the total distance in centimeters moved in 2 days?',['0 ≤ x ≤ 2','(17)(0.5) ≤ x ≤ (24)(0.5)','17 ≤ x ≤ 24','(17)(2) ≤ x ≤ (24)(2)'],'D','Multiply both bounds on the daily distance by 2: 34 ≤ x ≤ 48.')
a(1,'M1',14,49,'pct','One leuga equals 7,500 pedes. How many pedes equal 4.6 leugas?',None,'34500','7500 × 4.6 = 34500.',check='7500*4.6 == 34500')
a(1,'M1',15,49,'quad','A rectangle has width n yards and length (n + 7) yards. Its area is 198 square yards. What is n?',None,'11','n(n+7)=198 gives (n−11)(n+18)=0. A width is positive, so n=11.',check='11*(11+7) == 198')
a(1,'M1',16,49,'eq',r'For an object of mass 55 kg, \(55=\frac{2K}{v^2}\), where K and v are positive. Which equation expresses its speed v in terms of kinetic energy K?',[r'\(v=\frac{2K}{55^2}\)',r'\(v=\frac{55^2}{2K}\)',r'\(v=\sqrt{\frac{55}{2K}}\)',r'\(v=\sqrt{\frac{2K}{55}}\)'],'D','Multiply by v² and divide by 55: v²=2K/55. Since v>0, take the positive square root.')
