a(1,'M1',18,50,'exp','A company produced 7,138 peak kilowatts of solar cells in 2013. Production grew by approximately 22% each year for the following 5 years. Which function models production C(n), n years after 2013, for 0 ≤ n ≤ 5?',[r'\(C(n)=7138(0.22)^n\)',r'\(C(n)=7138(1.22)^n\)',r'\(C(n)=0.22(7138)^n\)',r'\(C(n)=1.22(7138)^n\)'],'B','A 22% annual increase multiplies the preceding value by 1.22. Initial value is 7138.')
a(1,'M1',19,50,'tri','In the right triangle shown, angles A and C are each 45°, angle B is 90°, and hypotenuse AC = x = 19. What is sin A?',[r'\(\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\)',r'\(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\)','1',r'\(\sqrt{2}\)'],'B','sin 45°=√2/2=1/√2. The side length 19 does not change this ratio.',[95,1080,315,1305])
a(1,'M1',20,51,'vol','A right square prism has height 15 units and volume 1,815 cubic units. What is the length of an edge of its square base?',None,'11','15s²=1815, so s²=121 and s=11.',check='15*11**2 == 1815')
a(1,'M1',21,51,'sys','A solution of y = x − 1 and y = 19(x − 1)² − 20 is (x,y). What is one possible value of x − 1?',['−2',r'\(-\frac{20}{19}\)','−1',r'\(-\frac{1}{19}\)'],'C','Let u=x−1. Then 19u²−u−20=0=(u+1)(19u−20), so u=−1 or 20/19. Only −1 is listed.')
a(1,'M1',22,51,'sys',r'The system is \(18x+6y=8y+9\) and \(ty=\frac{1}{5}+9x\). If the system has no solution, what is t?',None,'1','The first equation is y=9x−9/2. For t≠0 the second is y=(9/t)x+1/(5t). Equal slopes require t=1, and their intercepts differ. At t=0 the equations intersect, so t=1 is the required value.')
a(1,'M1',23,51,'cir','A circle has center (24,5) and y-intercepts (0,−27) and (0,37). What is its radius?',['40','37','32','27'],'A','Use the distance from (24,5) to (0,37): √(24²+32²)=40.',check='24**2+32**2 == 40**2')
a(1,'M1',24,52,'exp',r'For x>0, which expression is equivalent to \(\sqrt{x^3}\cdot\sqrt[4]{x}\)?',[r'\(x^{3/8}\)',r'\(x^{7/4}\)',r'\(x^{5/4}\)',r'\(x^{3/4}\)'],'B','Add the exponents: 3/2+1/4=7/4.')
