a(1,'M2E',12,56,'stat','A random sample of 42 locations in a state gives an estimated mean iced-coffee price of $1.37 with margin of error $0.05. Which is a plausible statement about the mean price for all locations selling iced coffee in the state?',['It is between $1.32 and $1.42.','It is either less than $1.32 or greater than $1.42.','It is less than $1.32.','It is greater than $1.42.'],'A','The estimate plus or minus the margin of error is $1.37±$0.05, or $1.32 to $1.42. This describes a plausible interval, not a certainty.')
a(1,'M2E',13,56,'eq','An assignment worth 10 points has x questions worth 1 point each and y questions worth 2 points each. Which equation represents the situation?',['3xy = 10','3(x + y) = 10','2x + y = 10','x + 2y = 10'],'D','The one-point questions contribute x points, and the two-point questions contribute 2y points.')
